  "analyzed_vuln": {
    "function": "ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM_SPEC_VAR_CV_OP_DATA_CONST_HANDLER",
    "file": "php-src/Zend/zend_vm_execute.h",
    "description": "Heap-use-after-free caused by re-entrant mutation of the assignment target during dimension assignment error handling. In ZEND_ASSIGN_DIM_SPEC_VAR_CV_OP_DATA_CONST_HANDLER, the handler converts false/null to array and then unconditionally calls zval_ptr_dtor_nogc(EX_VAR(opline->op1.var)) at the end. With this PoC, an undefined variable/index warning invokes user error handler that sets $GLOBALS['a']=null while the opcode is still executing. The original array zval for op1 is freed in that re-entrant path, but the opcode later performs destructor/refcount operations on the stale op1 zval, leading to UAF (seen in zend_gc_delref via zval_ptr_dtor_nogc). Crash is observed in JIT trace execution of the corresponding TMP variant, but root cause is unsafe lifetime handling in ASSIGN_DIM handlers under re-entrant error handler side effects.",
    "conditions": "Trigger requires ASSIGN_DIM on a CV/VAR where warning-producing dimension access occurs (e.g., undefined index/offset) and a user error handler that mutates/frees the same global variable being assigned (here $a). Data flow: fuzzer input PHP script installs set_error_handler, performs $a[$c] operations that raise warnings, handler sets $GLOBALS['a']=null, freeing array allocated earlier in ASSIGN_DIM path; execution then resumes and opcode/JIT handler decrefs/dtors stale zval from EX_VAR(op1), causing heap UAF."
  },
